 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: \"Dies kund zu thun\" in three words and the old spelling \"thun\", Tamino's \"sagt mir an\" (the libretto has \"saget an\") and \"Kleinen\" without a comma, and the repeat of the music (\"dann, Jüngling, wirst du männlich siegen\" twice). Each boy has his own line; the print puts the First and Second Boys on one staff, and Tamino on the Third Boy's staff. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
